For a triple $(z_1,z_2,z_3)$, construct a Möbius transformation $alpha$ sending it to $(0,1,oo)$ by
$alpha(z) = ((z_2 - z_3)/(z_2-z_1))(z - z_1)/(z - z_3)$,
with the cases involving $oo$ modified appropriately. Construct $beta$ similarly for $(w_1,w_2,w_3)$. Then $beta^(-1) compose alpha$ sends $z_i$ to $w_i$. Uniqueness follows from the three-point lemma.
